1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,265
Low tide returned the money Jason had
thrown away. Lucia wished the harbor

2
00:00:05,265 --> 00:00:07,290
had kept its mouth shut.

3
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:11,745
The transparent pouch lay tangled
beneath the public pier, where he'd

4
00:00:11,745 --> 00:00:13,770
dropped it after their argument.

5
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:18,634
They stood above it, waiting. Back then,
keeping the money had meant

6
00:00:18,634 --> 00:00:19,850
breaking a promise.

7
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:25,115
Now their rent was late. Jason climbed
down the public steps and lifted

8
00:00:25,115 --> 00:00:27,140
the pouch from the mud.

9
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:31,595
Lucia said nothing. He counted through
the plastic, lips moving, already

10
00:00:31,595 --> 00:00:34,430
rebuilding the life that money could
buy.

11
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:39,702
Then a marina worker pointed to the
donation box for storm repairs. Its

12
00:00:39,702 --> 00:00:41,730
glass front held three coins.

13
00:00:41,730 --> 00:00:46,995
Jason looked from the pouch to Lucia. He
pushed it through the collection

14
00:00:46,995 --> 00:00:48,210
slot before reconsidering.

15
00:00:48,210 --> 00:00:54,269
They walked home with wet shoes and the
same overdue rent. This time, the

16
00:00:54,269 --> 00:00:56,000
money stayed thrown away.
